  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "3062f2bbf16433b97e7090d1a4317b8c389bfe87",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 525908622,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> The DECT dissector currently does not call the `register_dissector` method. Therefore, the dissector cannot be called as sub-dissector.\n\nIt cannot be called *directly*, but if there's a dissector table in which it can be registered with a numerical or string key, it can be called through that.\n\n> This merge request registers the DECT dissector correctly.\n\nThere's nothing inherently incorrect about not registering a dissector by name.  Registering it with a name is for cases where a given dissector always calls another specific dissector, so there's no reason to have a dissector table from which the first dissector picks another dissector to call, or where the dissector to call isn't determined by a simple mechanism such as a table with integers or strings as keys.\n\nFrom what dissector are you planning to call the DECT dissector?  A comment at the beginning of the DECT dissector says:\n\n```\n/*\n TODO (roughly in that order)\n - Expand beyond full slot, 2-level modulation\n - Make things stateful\n - Once the capture format has stabilized, get rid of the Ethernet\n   hack and use a proper capture type.\n */\n```\n\nIs this part of \"Once the capture format has stabilized, get rid of the Ethernet hack and use a proper capture type.\"?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-10T09:13:26.316Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-10T09:13:26.316Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 91460181,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
